Design a simple register-based read interface that outputs a 32-bit read data value based on a 2-bit address input. The module reads data from an input port when the address is 0 and guarantees that the output is reset to zero when the reset signal is asserted low. The design includes a clock-enabled mechanism that updates the output on the rising edge of the clock, ensuring synchronous operation while allowing for a single data source via a multiplexer.
