Design a binary counter that takes an 8-bit input and produces an 8-bit output. The circuit first performs a bitwise AND operation between the input bits and logic high (1), effectively passing the input unchanged. It then sums this result with itself using an adder, effectively doubling the value of the input. The least significant 8 bits of the sum are assigned to the output, providing a dynamic output based on the input value. This module effectively counts in binary by doubling the given input.
