Design a circuit that converts a 3-bit binary input into the corresponding 7-segment display signals. For each binary value from 0 to 7, the circuit outputs specific signals to the segments (a, b, c, d, e, f, g) to represent the digits 0 through 7 on a 7-segment display. The module includes a default case that turns off all segments for any invalid input, ensuring that no erroneous patterns are displayed.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] in,
    output reg a, b, c, d, e, f, g
);

